This is supported in Material UI v5.

Use the public `useThemeProps` export together with `styled` metadata:

```tsx
import { styled, useThemeProps } from '@mui/material/styles';

const MyCustomComponentRoot = styled('div', {
  name: 'MuiMyCustomComponent',
  slot: 'Root',
})<{ variant?: 'dashed'; color?: 'secondary' }>({});

export function MyCustomComponent(inProps) {
  const props = useThemeProps({
    props: inProps,
    name: 'MuiMyCustomComponent',
  });

  return <MyCustomComponentRoot {...props} />;
}
```

`useThemeProps` applies `defaultProps`; `styled` with the same `name` applies the theme’s `styleOverrides` and `variants`. Then configure:

```ts
createTheme({
  components: {
    MuiMyCustomComponent: {
      defaultProps: { variant: 'dashed' },
      variants: [
        {
          props: { variant: 'dashed' },
          style: { border: '2px dashed' },
        },
